":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4123940326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117741#issuecomment-4123940326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117741","id":4123940326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71zlXm","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-25T05:44:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T22:17:03Z","body":"Still not sure about `get_latency()`, but I've added support for many different formats of hardware. I moved the initialization of the sndio driver after the pulse and alsa drivers because is it probably the least likely to be present, but I also just realized it does not require an `sndiod` server running to function and can attach directly to hardware given the correct permissions meaning that the server does not have to be running in order to attempt opening a device. The pulse driver for example will fail if there is no running PulseAudio server.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"u